# Force LF for files that run inside Linux containers or are parsed by a
# shebang interpreter. Without this, a Windows checkout with the common
# `core.autocrlf=true` setting silently rewrites LF to CRLF on every clone
# or `git worktree add`, which corrupts a script's shebang line (`env`
# resolves the interpreter name literally, so `bash\r` does not exist) and
# breaks the container at start time with no diff ever showing in `git
# status`. See docker/backend entrypoint failure investigated in Phase 2.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are edited and run on Windows; CRLF is their native and
# expected line ending (and Windows PowerShell 5.1 has known issues with
# non-ASCII characters in LF-only/BOM-less files - see .ai/HANDOFF.md).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
